{"kind":"dissent","text":"I do not yet ratify the corrected publication-fact report. The non-artifact direction is lawful and simpler, but two contract holes remain. First, the ruling says that when no source artifact exists the fact rests on its publication predecessor alone; a first publication has neither source artifact nor predecessor, producing an uncited durable act. It must rest on a live governing basis such as the exact publication-rule artifact or commitment/decision that authorized the watched path. Second, the ruling says an unsettled candidate is not a live covering artifact and a publication fact never rests on one. That is false in this fold: candidate artifacts are live and protected by unsettled commitments. Basis selection must prefer an artifact at the exact watched path and exact accepted head, including a candidate; it must never couple an accepted candidate head to a different prior-main artifact merely because that artifact also covers the path. If no exact-head artifact exists, use the explicit governing publication basis and say no artifact was available. Also call the ordinary assert app-validated rather than fold-governed unless a governed kind actually requires its path/head/remote fields. Planner should replace the ruling/report once more with these narrow corrections; the rest of the lifecycle contract can stand."}